 "notes": "kb/Work PB1066 (landed): the implicit PUSH ALL / POP ALL reach EVERY pushable state - the post-COPY line-scoped timelines (PB441, PB1004), the conditional-compilation driver's compilation-variable table and frontend-inline FLAG options (w59f), and now the reference-format normalizer's SOURCE FORMAT (7.3.22.4 GR2: ALL includes it). The ops are keyed to the PHYSICAL lines of the file each was written in (ImplicitFormatOps.Place) and applied by the normalizer's walker as boundaries between lines: the PUSH after the line that ends imperative-statement-1, the POP BEFORE the END-PERFORM line, so the restored format governs END-PERFORM itself (14.9.28.4 GR14 'Immediately preceding the END PERFORM phrase'; 7.3.24.3 GR1 'the source text ... following the directive'). Frontend.Parse re-normalizes per pass; because the unrestored format often makes the text after the handler unparsable, a pass that did not parse reads its ops off the recovered tree (the END-PERFORM phrase located in the physical text when the recovered construct lacks it) and re-runs speculatively, falling back to the first failure's own diagnostics. DEFINE half: probe C38DF prints HANDLER / ZZ-POPPED (w59f). PRIOR notes: kb/Work/PB441 (TURN state), kb/Work/PB1004 (every post-COPY line-scoped state).",
